{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Measured as the policy requires — the governing figure is the trace, gps_trace.trace_distance_km of 17.08 km against the booked optimal of 13.9 km — the excess is 3.18 km, or 22.88%. That clears POL-RD-01's two establishment gates (0.8 km and 20%), but it is nowhere near the materiality gates of 8.0 km and 50%, so this is at most an ordinary threshold-level deviation and not a MATERIAL one; the materiality-triggered machinery of POL-RD-01 does not engage.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00530"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no repeat-deviation pattern to convert a modest excess into a full refund. driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0, below the clause's threshold of 3, and 0 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 250 is 0, far below the 0.05 ratio and with well over the 40 trips the test requires. POL-RD-06's pattern consequences — in particular the FULL_REFUND uplift and the driver-conduct referral — therefore do not arise, and the profile cannot be used to build a pattern finding against the driver.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00530"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's account is that a bus breakdown blocked the main road, so he took Balestier. But this record contains no advisory at all: EV-ADVIS-00530-01 is MISSING, flagged MISSING_ARTIFACT (severity BLOCKING) and carrying weight 0.0 — it can prove no fact, and its absence is itself citable. Without a traffic_advisory the POL-RD-03 test cannot be run, and POL-RD-10(5) makes a closure asserted with no traffic_advisory a mandatory escalation trigger. The correct disposition on this record is therefore ESCALATE: the disputed amount is HELD rather than refunded while a human reviews it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00530-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10", "POL-RD-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's narrative is habit and a fare comparison, not a distance measurement: it says the trip usually costs 'around fifty dollars' and that this taxi came to 'seventy-six', yet the ledger records SGD 26.95 charged for this very trip. The rider's own figures do not correspond to the record, and an allegation of a repeated pattern — 'how many times did I NOT check?' — that identifies no other trip and cites no other artifact carries no weight under POL-RD-08; the only measure of deviation the policy recognises is the distance derived from this trip's own trace.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00530", "EV-TRIP-00530"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider contests the entire SGD 26.95, but POL-RD-02 is arithmetic, not discretionary, and it caps any recovery. On the metered fare the recomputed figure is 21.1850 (base 3.80 plus 0.75 x 13.9 km plus 0.28 x 22 min = 20.385, at a surge multiplier of 1.0 read from the fare_breakdown, plus the 0.80 platform fee), so the refund before rounding is 5.765 against a charged total of 26.95 — a refund share of 21.4%, far below the 90% FULL_REFUND threshold and with reaches_full_refund_share recorded as false. The rider's demand for the whole fare cannot be met on any view of this policy.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00530"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.recomputed_fare",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.0,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver — this trip's measurements are clear, but the record cannot test the driver's excuse, so a human reviewer must decide it; the disputed SGD 26.95 is HELD rather than collected or refunded.\n\nThe deviation is established. The governing figure is the GPS trace (EV-GPS-00530): 17.08 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff against the booked optimal of 13.9 km (EV-TRIP-00530), an excess of 3.18 km — 22.88% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 gates pass (0.8 km and 20%), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED; it is below the material gates (8.0 km / 50%), so POL-RD-01's material machinery and POL-RD-06's pattern check never engage — the driver's 90-day counters are 0 deviation flags over 250 completed trips, no pattern, so no FULL_REFUND uplift and no conduct referral arise. The trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07 (205 fixes at 10 s cadence, no gap over 90 s, no jump over 500 m, max gap 0 s), so the excess needs no independent corroboration. Nothing exonerates any part of it: the chat log is empty so POL-RD-04 cannot run, no endpoint was amended so POL-RD-05 cannot run, and this is RYDE_TAXI, not a pooled trip, so POL-RD-12 does not apply. POL-RD-11 has no purchase (fare model METERED, quoted fare null).\n\nOn the merits the arithmetic would give the rider a partial refund, and I record the figure so the reviewer has it: under POL-RD-02 the recomputed fare is (3.80 + 0.75 x 13.9 + 0.28 x 22.0) x 1.0 (surge read from the fare_breakdown) + 0.80 platform fee = 21.185, and the refund is 26.95 - 21.185 = 5.765, i.e. SGD 5.80, which is 21.4% of the charge — above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and below the 90% full-refund share.\n\nWhy the case escalates. The driver's account is that a bus breakdown forced him via Balestier. That is an exculpatory claim under POL-RD-03, which requires a traffic_advisory naming a road the optimal route traverses, in a validity window overlapping the trip, matched by the vehicle leaving and rejoining the optimal corridor. No such advisory exists here: EV-ADVIS-00530-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT (severity BLOCKING), recording that no advisory covers the optimal corridor in this window. POL-RD-10(5) makes a closure asserted with no traffic_advisory a mandatory escalation, so the driver's excuse can neither be accepted nor rejected on this record — a human must obtain the advisory records for that corridor and window (or establish that none was issued) before POL-RD-03 can be run. The driver's other point, that a metered taxi costs more than the app's discount cars, is not a defence: POL-RD-01 measures the excess against the platform's optimal route for the booked product, not against another product tier. I do not accept the rider's contention that no POL-RD-10 trigger fires — the absent advisory is exactly the (5) case. Because the only artifact bearing on that trigger, EV-ADVIS-00530-01, is MISSING at weight 0.0, my confidence is capped at 0.0 under POL-GEN-02(2); that is itself below the policy's 0.70 floor, so POL-RD-10(1) is engaged as well. The finding that the deviation is established is unaffected by that cap.\n\nWhat the reviewer should do: confirm whether any traffic advisory covered the optimal corridor during 08:06-08:41 on 18 Sep 2026. If one exists, run POL-RD-03 (removing any justified excess) and recompute under POL-RD-02; if none exists, the deviation stands as established and the merits figure is the SGD 5.80 partial refund to the rider.",
    "referrals": []
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "Once the rider has shown the threshold excess the burden is the driver's, and POL-RD-08 is explicit that a general assertion that traffic was bad, unsupported by a traffic_advisory ID, does not discharge it. No advisory ID, no closure record and no admission of an unjustified detour appears anywhere in this record, so nothing rebuts the established deviation.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00530-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.7,
    "explanation": "This is a metered taxi trip (TRP-00530, RYDE_TAXI) from Hougang to Raffles Place. I cannot issue a final money ruling on this record. The SGD 26.95 is held — not refunded to the rider and not retained by the driver — pending human review.\n\nWhat is established, for both parties. Measured the way POL-RD-01 requires — on gps_trace.trace_distance_km (17.08 km), and not on the trip record's rounded 17.1 km copy, which the clause forbids citing for the threshold test — the distance driven exceeded the booked optimal of 13.9 km by 3.18 km, or 22.88%. That passes both establishment gates (0.8 km and 20%), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED. It does not reach the materiality gates (8.0 km or 50%), so the POL-RD-06 materiality machinery is not engaged. The trace is clean — 205 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps, max_gap_sec 0 — so it is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a)–(c) and needs no independent corroboration. The driver's 90-day counters (0 deviation flags over 250 completed trips) show no repeat pattern, so neither the FULL_REFUND uplift nor a POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral arises.\n\nWhy the case cannot be finally ruled. The driver's account is that a bus breakdown on the main road forced the Balestier route. That is an assertion of an external traffic event, and only POL-RD-03 can excuse it — but POL-RD-03 requires a traffic_advisory naming a road or segment the optimal route traverses, within the trip window. There is none. EV-ADVIS-00530-01 is MISSING, carries weight 0.0 and fired the BLOCKING issue MISSING_ARTIFACT. Its absence is citable, but the consequence is that the driver's excuse can neither be confirmed nor dismissed on this record. I do not accept the rider's submission that this absence merely 'defeats his excuse' and leaves the case decidable: where an exculpatory clause is invoked and the artifact it depends on is missing from the pool — the policy's own example is 'a closure asserted with no traffic_advisory' — POL-RD-10(5) makes escalation mandatory. No monetary outcome therefore issues and the disputed amount is held.\n\nWhat would resolve it. A traffic_advisory valid for 18 September 2026, covering approximately 08:06–08:41 SGT, naming a road or segment on the optimal Hougang–Raffles Place corridor, together with the shortest lawful alternative distance if a closure is claimed, would let POL-RD-03 be run and this case be decided on its merits.\n\nClaim points that do not change the outcome. The driver's second point — that a taxi meter is dearer than the app's discount cars — is not a defence under any clause: POL-RD-01 measures the excess against the platform's optimal route for the booked product, not against the price of a different product tier. No rider-requested detour applies (the chat log has zero messages and no waypoint_hint, POL-RD-04); no endpoint was amended (pickup_amended_at, dropoff_amended_at and amended_optimal_distance_km are all null, POL-RD-05); and this is not a pooled trip (RYDE_TAXI, not RYDE_POOL, POL-RD-12). The fare model is METERED with a null quoted fare, so POL-RD-11 has no purchase. There are no ERP or surcharge lines in the fare breakdown to correct under POL-RD-09 (erp total 0.00, airport surcharge 0.00), and the rider's history factor under POL-RD-08 does not engage (deviation_claims_60d 0). The rider's narrative of 'around fifty' versus 'seventy-six' is a fare comparison, not a distance measurement, and does not correspond to the SGD 26.95 charged on this trip.\n\nFor the reviewer's information only (not ordered today): had the case been decidable, POL-RD-02 on this METERED fare would give recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 × 13.9 + 0.28 × 22.0) × 1.0 + 0.80 = 21.185, so a refund of 26.95 − 21.185 = 5.765, rounded UP to SGD 5.80 — above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and 21.4% of charged_total, i.e. a PARTIAL_REFUND. The surge multiplier of 1.0 was read from the fare_breakdown, where the policy places it.\n\nConfidence 0.70: the deviation finding is carried by weight-1.0 artifacts (the GPS trace and the trip record), but the exculpatory limb turns on an artifact that is absent, so the merits cannot be resolved on this record."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "Once the rider has shown the threshold excess the burden is the driver's, and POL-RD-08 is explicit that a general assertion that traffic was bad, unsupported by a traffic_advisory ID, does not discharge it. No advisory ID, no closure record and no admission of an unjustified detour appears anywhere in this record, so nothing rebuts the established deviation.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00530-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}

